# 0.5 (backlog item 69), the OTHER half of 958: the same false drawing
# with NO author coordinate anywhere — no `layout`, no `pin`. Auto-layout puts
# "x" in the corridor between the two aggregated links, the lasso closes round
# it, and the figure states that the console is part of the LAG.
#
# The separation pass moves a non-member out of a lasso whenever there is free
# room to move it into, exactly as it already does for a group band. Here there
# is none: this lasso's ring falls back to the pre-0.4 derivation (the ring
# cannot clear the tap boxes its own members run through), and that shape's
# extent IS the members' fan — so "clear of the lasso" is precisely where t1
# and t2 already are, on both sides. The pass declines rather than shove the
# figure into an overlap or off the canvas, and the rule reports in the band's
# own "could not separate" voice.
figdown 0.4 topology
title "A lasso the layout closed round a bystander"
node a "Switch A"
node t1 "Tap 1"
node x "Console"
node t2 "Tap 2"
node b "Switch B"
edge a -- t1
edge t1 -- b
edge a -- x
edge x -- b
edge a -- t2
edge t2 -- b
bundle lag "LAG" a--t1,t1--b,a--t2,t2--b
